otal lines: 81\nL0@P0: 2. Registration Number\nL1@P0: 7518\nL2@P0: To correct a deficiency in\nL3@P0: Initial Statement\nL4@P0: To give notice of change in an exhibit previously filed.\nL5@P0: subsidiary of Israel Aerospace industries, Ltd.,\nL6@P0: Register for Foreign Principal 'stark Aerospace inc. (Israel)'\nL7@P0: Received by NSD/FARA Registration Unit 12/12/2025 10:57:35 AM\nL8@P0: INSTRUCTIONS. File this amendment form for any changes to a registration. Compliance is accomplished by filing an electronic amendment to\nL9@P0: registration statement and uploading any supporting documents at https://www.fara.gov.\nL10@P0: Privacy Act Statement. The filing ofthis document is required for the Foreign Agents Registration Act of 1938, as amended, 22 U.S.C. § 611 erseq.,\nL11@P0: for the purposes ofregistration under the Act and public disclosure. Provision ofthe information requested is mandatory, and failure to provide the\nL12@P0: information is subject to the penalty and enforcement provisions established in Section 8 ofthe Act. Eveiy registration statement, short form\nL13@P0: registration statement, supplemental statement, exhibit, amendment, copy ofinformational materials or other document or information filed with the\nL14@P0: Attorney General under this Act is a public record open to public examination, inspection and copying during the posted business hours ofthe\nL15@P0: FARA Unit in Washington, DC. Statements are also available online at the FARA Unit’s webpage: https://www.fara.gov. One copy ofeveiy such\nL16@P0: document, other than informational materials, is automatically provided to the Secretary of State pursuant to Section 6(b) ofthe Act, and copies of\nL17@P0: any and all documents are routinely made available to other agencies, departments and Congress pursuant to Section 6(c) ofthe Act. The Attorney\nL18@P0: General also transmits a semi-annual report to Congress on the administration ofthe Act which lists the names of all agents registered under the Act\nL19@P0: and the foreign principals they represent. This report is available to the public online at: https://www.fara.gov.\nL20@P0: Public Reporting Burden. Public reporting burden for this collection ofinformation is estimated to average .75 hours per response, including the\nL21@P0: tune for reviewing instructions, searching existing data sources, gathering and maintaining the data needed, and completing and reviewing the\nL22@P0: collection ofinformation. Send comments regarding this burden estimate or any other aspect ofthis collection ofinformation, including suggestions\nL23@P0: for reducing this burden to Chief, FARA Unit, Counterintelligence and Export Control Section, National Security Division, U.S. Department of\nL24@P0: Justice, Washington, DC 20530; and to the Office ofInformation and Regulatory Affairs, Office ofManagement and Budget, Washington, DC 20503.\nL25@P0: 5. Each item checked above must be explained below m full detail together with, where appropriate, specific reference to and identity\nL26@P0: ofthe item in the registration statement to which it pertains.\nL27@P0: FORM NSD-5\nL28@P0: Revised 10/23\nL29@P0: Adding new foreign principal, stark Aerospace Inc.\nL30@P0: a parastatal entity of the Government of Israel.\nL31@P0: 4. Ifthis amendment requires the filing of a document or documents, please list:\nL32@P0: Exhibit a to Registration statement\nL33@P0: Exhibit B to Registration statement\nL34@P0: Short Form to Registration statement\nL35@P0: 1. Name ofRegistrant\nL36@P0: GlobalPoint international\nL37@P0: U.S. Department of Justice\nL38@P0: Washington, DC 20530\nL39@P0: Supplemental Statement for the 6 month period ending\nL40@P0: Other purpose (specify)\nL41@P0: 3. This amendment is filed to accomplish the following indicated purpose(es):\nL42@P0: g To give notice ofchange in information as required by Section 2(b) ofthe Act.\nL43@P0: Received by NSD/FARA Registration Unit 12/12/2025 10:57:35 AM\nL44@P0: OMB No. 1124-0003; Expi